/red/pull/21.patch","merged_at":"2026-06-26T19:23:15Z"},"body":"## Summary\n\n- Restore Red's CSS theme tokens on current `main` after the recent identity/template sync left the public accent and primary colors on the template blue hue.\n- Updates light and dark `--primary`, `--ring`, `--accent-*`, `--sidebar-primary`, and `--sidebar-ring` values to the red brand hue.\n\n## What changed on main\n\nCurrent `origin/main` includes PR #16 (`feat(identity): set repo-spec intent — hook + mission + brand{icon,color}`), which correctly set `.cogni/repo-spec.yaml` to `brand.color: \"#ef4444\"`, but `app/src/styles/tailwind.css` still had blue `217` tokens. That is why the live page showed a red icon but blue `/red`, headline gradient, CTA button, and spinner/accent controls.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Fetched current `origin/main` before patching.\n- Static token check passed for light/dark primary, ring, and accent variables.\n\n## Note\n\nLocal `typecheck` and dev rendering are currently blocked on unrelated `origin/main` package/export issues in `repoSpec.server.ts` / `@cogni/repo-spec`, before this CSS change is involved.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cogni-dao/red/issues/21/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cogni-dao/red/issues/21/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]]